From 7e014e776a7089406c799017c62d2cc6cf86e14f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stein Milder <info@steinmilder.nl>
Date: Sat, 15 Aug 2026 23:30:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: ti: add SoundTap ST10 McASP machine driver

The SoundTap ST10 uses McASP with a simple audio codec endpoint, fixed at
48 kHz stereo and 32-bit samples. Add the board-specific machine driver
that configures the required clocks, format, and TDM slots. Build it
unconditionally to preserve the legacy NAND image build behavior.

The driver source itself is os/drivers/soundtap-st10-audio.c, copied into
sound/soc/ti/ by SOUNDTAP_LINUX_MCASP_DRIVER (os/external.mk) after the
patches apply; this patch only builds it. One copy, so the WLA can no
longer get a stale driver (its bose,soundtap-mcasp-spdif match once went
missing from a second copy and the board had no audio at all).

Upstream: Not applicable (SoundTap hardware support)
Signed-off-by: Stein Milder <info@steinmilder.nl>
---
 sound/soc/ti/Makefile | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/sound/soc/ti/Makefile b/sound/soc/ti/Makefile
index 421e13bc04db..5ca646d16e6c 100644
--- a/sound/soc/ti/Makefile
+++ b/sound/soc/ti/Makefile
@@ -44,3 +44,4 @@ obj-$(CONFIG_SND_SOC_OMAP_AMS_DELTA) += snd-soc-ams-delta.o
 obj-$(CONFIG_SND_SOC_OMAP_HDMI) += snd-soc-omap-hdmi.o
 obj-$(CONFIG_SND_SOC_OMAP_OSK5912) += snd-soc-osk5912.o
 obj-$(CONFIG_SND_SOC_J721E_EVM) += snd-soc-j721e-evm.o
+obj-y += soundtap-st10-audio.o
